mptcp-bpf-first (1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fall back to the first usable subflow when msk->first cannot send. The
    scheduler keeps its single-path character -- msk->first is still used
    whenever it can carry data -- but no longer insists on a subflow whose WAN
    is blackholed, which stopped transfers for as long as TCP took to give up
    (measured as a 24 s stall and 3.6x the payload on the wire).

 -- Yannick Chabanois <contact@openmptcprouter.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

